{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe carriage rattled us to Duxan by four, half-way to Töplitz. The innkeeper, a stout Bohemian named Kral, insisted we stay, citing the mist closing in over the Elbe. He was right; the view from the window is grey and flat, a perfect mirror of my mood after eating cold mutton. The wine is thin, but the snuff is excellent. I paid three florins for the room and dinner; a fair price for the dust.\n\nKarl’s letter reached me in Prague. I see he has begun his studies. Tell him to listen to his instructors, not his own cleverness. Obedience is the soil in which judgment grows. Do not let Ludwig linger too long at the café; I want him walking with me tomorrow.\n\nThe mist is thickening. I will sleep soon. Kiss the boys for me.\n\nYour\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795219118,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":197,"prompt_tokens":1070,"total_tokens":1267,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-nR0jyVFd2owNxGFiE7f9T2GBTStnO7q9","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1070,"prompt_ms":1065.04,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9953644859813083,"prompt_per_second":1004.6571020806731,"predicted_n":197,"predicted_ms":4615.816,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.55008163265306,"predicted_per_second":42.462697819843775}}